    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0822" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg688"/>

                <head>No. 503.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 7, 1888</date>.
                        (Received January 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 652.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have tho honor to inclose herewith a
                    report by Mr. Henry White, first secretary of this legation, upon the
                    proceedings of the <pb facs="0823" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/> international
                    conference recently held here in reference to the question of sugar bounties, at
                    which he was directed by you to be present.</p>
                <p>This report is so full and satisfactory that I do not deem it necessary or useful
                    to add anything thereto.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d503-a1.xml" xpointer="d503-a1"/>
